      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Imperial%2C_Texas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Water from the Pecos River was diverted and a small dam built west of the community to support irrigation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Imperial%2C_Texas",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "An irrigation canal was later constructed through Imperial, but high salt content made farming unproductive, leading to a population decline.",
